<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n16560" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">exaltātĭo</span></b> ,
			ōnis, f.
		exalto. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Exaltation</i>, <i>elevation</i>
			(eccl. Lat.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ab exaltatione tua dispersae sunt gentes,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg.
					Isa. 33, 3</span></i>
			. —</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>, <i>pride</i>, <i>haughtiness</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">non congruit professoribus humilitatis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tert. Cult. Fem. 3</span></i>
			; cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">oculorum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg.
					Prov. 21, 4</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">stultorum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 3, 35</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
